  "limitations": [
    "No paid model requests. DeepSeek image payload, capability and provider probe guards were tested offline; actual account permissions and response quality were not verified.",
    "No real TapNow/WeChat account login, image generation or publication. Live external-page observations were limited to 10 seconds; live captures timed out in the final run. Controlled native navigation/download/popup/session isolation checks passed. An earlier source run loaded the TapNow /home page with 2016 visible characters (docs/v1.2-browser-source-debug.log).",
    "Docker was not installed in this environment. Isolated execution authorization and sample-input preparation were tested with a controlled runner, not a real Docker daemon.",
    "Local host execution of new code still needs human review; TapNow image generation and WeChat publication are manual. Automatic real screenshots include all article run records and need final correspondence/crop review.",
    "The v1.1.1 installer shutdown/workspace-preservation hooks are retained. Their earlier isolated NSIS upgrade acceptance was not repeated with v1.2.0. The final installer payload was extracted and matched to the verified program; the user installation/workspace was not changed.",
    "Commercial signing is not configured."
  ],
  "resolved_during_acceptance": [
    "Browser mounting now has a separate animation-frame token from bounds updates; scroll/resize cannot cancel opening the view. Scroll state is reset on entry and two renderer regression cases cover the race.",
    "UI repacking moves existing archives aside before rebuilding, preventing electron-builder from treating a stale ZIP as current. Actual installer and ZIP payloads are hash-verified."
  ]
